where | | denotes the value of the field K. In the case of complex numbers the above
data and the leading coefficients a0 uniquely determine the polynomial g (y) up to the
translations, the rotations and the reflection. In the case of a non-archimedean valued
field K the above data give some weak but valuable Information about the polynomial

      Let the valued field K be k ((t)) the meromorphic field of one variable and the
polynomial g(y) be irreducible over K. Then it can be shown that the configuration
data of g(y) over its Splitting field is equivalent to the classical data of the characteristic
pairs of an algebroid curve.

