+(`denominator of order delta <= u_s = 3`) and prints the degree-`u_s` leading
+polynomial framework in Prop. 7.3 / Section 8.  The missing proof is the
+standard Puiseux Galois action on the ramified parameter at the split.  The
+action used here is `mu_e` on `t^(1/e)`, not Moh p.201(8)'s major-disc
+denominator-increment action.  Moh p.201 is only an analogue.
+
+`NOT[N5-DIVIDES]`: N5 is an inequality, not divisibility.  The source-surviving
+case `delta=5/2`, `e=2`, `u_s=3`, with Galois-stable
+`p(pi)=pi(pi^2-c)`, shows `e` need not divide `u_s`.
+
